# One canonical line ending everywhere. The engine's text formats (canonical YAML writer,
# golden files, schema exports) are byte-compared in tests; CRLF/LF drift across the
# Windows + macOS matrix would make byte-equality flap. LF is the canonical form.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never undergo EOL conversion — committed textures (and, later, golden
# images) are byte-exact. `text=auto` already detects these by content; this is explicit.
*.png binary
# The Rust-encoder/TS-decoder frame-codec fixtures (crates/ludion-server/examples/gen_frame_fixtures.rs,
# editor/app/src/protocol/__fixtures__/) are byte-compared in tests too — same reasoning.
*.qoi binary
*.lz4 binary
*.rgba binary
# Committed session recordings (LRP1, zstd-framed) — e.g. games/breakout/run.lrp.
*.lrp binary
# Committed PCM sound effects (decoded byte-exactly in tests) — e.g. hello-paddle's bounce.wav.
*.wav binary
# Committed font faces (bake inputs, read byte-exactly; examples/gallery/fonts/).
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
# Committed glTF buffers and binaries (games/vigil/art/town/kits/*/export/).
*.bin binary
*.glb binary
